000200 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000300 PROGRAM-ID.          TUMCF.
000400 AUTHOR.              C HILLES.
000500 DATE-WRITTEN.        DEC 18,1984.
000600 DATE-COMPILED.
000700*INSTALLATION.        GOODYEAR TIRE AND RUBBER - AKRON.
000800*SECURITY.
000900*REMARKS.
001000*
001100* THIS SUBPROGRAM IS USED TO CONVERT QUANTITES FROM 1 UNIT OF
001200* MEASURE TO OTHER UNITS OF MEASURE.  GIVEN A QUANTITY FOR
001300* A CORPORATE CODE AND THE UM FOR THAT QUANTITY, (AS WELL AS THE
001400* UMs AND UM CONVERSION FACTORS FOR THAT CODE), THIS SUBPROGRAM
001500* WILL RETURN THAT QUANTITY IN THE STOREROOM UNIT OF MEASURE AND
001600* THE TWO ALTERNATE UNIT OF MEASURES.  IN ADDITION, IT WILL
001700* CONVERT A QUANITITY FROM ONE GIVEN UNIT OF MEASURE TO ANOTHER
001800* GIVEN UNIT OF MEASURE.  ANY UM PASSED MUST BE ONE OF THE
001900* 3 POSSIBLE UNIT OF MEASURES FOR THAT CORPORATE CODE.  IF NOT,
002000* AN ERROR IS RETURNED.
002100*
002200* SPECIAL KELLY NOTE:
002300* IN KELLY PLANTS, PURCHASING PASSES THE QUANTITY ORDERED AND
002400* CONVERTS THAT QTY TO STOREROOM UM.  THE CONVERSION FACTOR IS
002500* DETERMINED FROM THESE 2 QUANTITIES - REGARDLESS OF WHAT MIGHT
002600* BE IN THE STOREROOM ALTERNATE UM FIELDS.  THIS CONVERSION FACTOR
002700* IS USED FOR PRICE CONVERSION.
002800*
002900*--------------------- PARAMETERS --------------------------------
003000*
003100* RET-CODE           PASS:
003200*                    'PR' TO CONVERT PRICES
003300*                    SPACES TO CONVERT QUANTITIES
003400*
003500*                    RETURN:
003600*                    'NF' = SOURCE UM WAS INVALID
003700*                    'ND' = DEST UM WAS INVALID
003800*
003900* STR-UM-AREA        X(16).  THIS IS THE STANDARD UNIT OF MEASURE
004000*                    AREA IN THE "MSTORERM" DATASET, DEFINED AS
004100*                    FOLLOWS:
004200*                       05  STR-UM      X(2).
004300*                       05  STR-UM1     X(2).
004400*                       05  STR-UM1-CF  S9(6)V9(4).
004500*                       05  STR-UM2     X(2).
004600*                       05  STR-UM2-CF  S9(6)V9(4).
004700*
004800* QTY-AREA.        X(72).  THIS AREA IS PASSED/RETURNED, AND IS
004900*                  SUB-DEFINED AS FOLLOWS:
005000*
005100* SOURCE-QTY       X(2). PASS THE QUANTITY OF THE ITEM YOU WISH
005200*                  CONVERTED.
005300*
005400* SOURCE-UM        X(2).  PASS THE KNOWN UNIT OF MEASURE OF THE
005500*                  ITEM YOU WISH CONVERTED.
005600*
005700* DEST-QTY         S9(8)V9(4).  THE QUANITY IN THE DESTINATION
005800*                  UNIT OF MEASURE WILL BE RETURNED.  THIS WILL
005900*                  ONLY BE RETURNED IF A DESTINATION UM IS PASSED.
006000*
006100* DEST-UM          X(2).  (OPTIONAL).  IF YOU WISH TO CONVERT FROM
006200*                  ONE UM TO ANOTHER SPECIFIC UM, PASS THE UM YOU
006300*                  WISH TO CONVERT TO HERE.  THE CONVERTED QUANTITY
006400*                  WILL BE RETURNED IN "DEST-QTY".
006500*
006600* QTY-STR-UM       S9(8).  THE QUANTITY IN THE STOREROOM UNIT OF
006700*                  MEASURE WILL BE RETURNED.  THE STOREROOM QUANTITY
006800*                  IS ALWAYS A WHOLE NUMBER (ROUNDING WILL BE DONE).
006900*
007000* QTY-STR-UM1      S9(8)V9(4).  THE QUANTITY IN THE FIRST ALTERNATE
007100*                  UM WILL BE RETURNED.
007200*
007300* QTY-STR-UM2      S9(8)V9(4).  THE QUANTITY IN THE SECOND ALTERNATE
007400*                  UM WILL BE RETURNED.
007500*
007600* QTY-STR-UM-DEC   S9(8)V9(4).  THE SAME AS "QTY-STR-UM", BUT WITH
007700*                  THE DECIMAL PART OF THE QUANTITY.
007800*
007900* KELLY-FLAG       PASS: 'Y' IF FOR KELLY CONVERSION LOGIC
008000*                        ANYTHING ELSE FOR NORMAL CONVERSION LOGIC
008100*
008200* KELLY-STR-QTY    PASS: IF KELLY CONVERSION, PASS A QUANTITY IN
008300*                  STR UM, THAT WILL BE EQUIVLENT TO THE ORDERED QTY
008400*                  IN ORD UM
008500*
008600* KELLY-ORD-QTY    PASS: IF KELLY CONVERSION, PASS A QUANTITY IN
008700*                  ORDERED UM, EQUIVILANT TO THE PASSED QUANTITY IN
008800*                  STR UM
008900*
009000* KELLY-ORD-UM     PASS: THE KELLY ORDER UNIT OF MEASURE
009100*                  (SEE SPECIAL KELLY NOTE ABOVE)
009200*
009300 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
009400 CONFIGURATION SECTION.
009500 SOURCE-COMPUTER.  HP-3000.
009600 OBJECT-COMPUTER.  HP-3000.
009700
009800 DATA DIVISION.
009900 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
010000 77  SAVE-RET-CODE                 PIC X(2).
010100 01  UM-AREA.
010200     05  STR-UM                    PIC X(2).
010300     05  STR-UM1                   PIC X(2).
010400     05  STR-UM1-CF                PIC S9(6)V9(4).
010500     05  STR-UM2                   PIC X(2).
010600     05  STR-UM2-CF                PIC S9(6)V9(4).
010700
010800 LINKAGE SECTION.
010900
011000 01  RET-CODE                      PIC X(2).
011100
011200 01  PASSED-UM-AREA.
011300     05  PASSED-STR-UM             PIC X(2).
011400     05  PASSED-STR-UM1            PIC X(2).
011500     05  PASSED-STR-UM1-CF         PIC S9(6)V9(4).
011600     05  PASSED-STR-UM2            PIC X(2).
011700     05  PASSED-STR-UM2-CF         PIC S9(6)V9(4).
011800
011900 01  QUANTITY-AREA.
012000     05  SOURCE-QTY                PIC S9(11)V9(4).
012100     05  SOURCE-UM                 PIC X(2).
012200     05  DEST-QTY                  PIC S9(11)V9(4).
012300     05  DEST-UM                   PIC X(2).
012400     05  QTY-STR-UM                PIC S9(8).
012500     05  QTY-STR-UM1               PIC S9(11)V9(4).
012600     05  QTY-STR-UM2               PIC S9(11)V9(4).
012700     05  QTY-STR-UM-DEC            PIC S9(11)V9(4).
012800     05  KELLY-FLAG                PIC X(1).
012900     05  KELLY-STR-QTY             PIC S9(11)V9(4).
013000     05  KELLY-ORD-QTY             PIC S9(11)V9(4).
013100     05  KELLY-ORD-UM              PIC X(2).
013200
013300 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING          RET-CODE,
013400                                   PASSED-UM-AREA,
013500                                   QUANTITY-AREA.
013600
013700 6000-MAIN.
013800
013900*------- WE MOVE UM TO A SAVE AREA, BECAUSE THE VALUES MAY BE
014000*------- CHANGED IN THE CASE OF KELLY
014100     MOVE PASSED-UM-AREA           TO   UM-AREA.
014200
014300*------- UNLESS SOMETHING GOES WRONG, RETURN CODE WILL BE
014400*------- GOOD (ZERO).
014500     MOVE RET-CODE  TO  SAVE-RET-CODE.
014600     MOVE "00"  TO  RET-CODE.
014700
014800*------- FOR KELLY, DETERMINE THE CONVERSION FACTOR FROM ORDERED
014900*------- UM TO STR UM, THEN SET UP ALTERNATE UM 1 AS THE ORDERED UM
015000*------- WITH THE CF.  FROM THEN ON, THE PROGRAM SHOULD WORK AS
015100*------- FOR NORMAL PLANTS.
015200     IF KELLY-FLAG = "Y"
               IF KELLY-STR-QTY = ZERO OR KELLY-ORD-QTY = ZERO
                   MOVE 1                TO   STR-UM1-CF
               ELSE
015300             DIVIDE KELLY-STR-QTY BY KELLY-ORD-QTY
015400              GIVING STR-UM1-CF ROUNDED
               END-IF
015500         MOVE KELLY-ORD-UM         TO   STR-UM1
015600         MOVE SPACES               TO   STR-UM2
015700         MOVE ZERO                 TO   STR-UM2-CF.
015800
015900*------- CONVERT QUANTITY PASSED IN THE SOURCE UNIT OF MEASURE
016000*------- INTO THE STOREROOM UNIT OF MEASURE.
016100*------- NOTE:  FOR PRICES, THE PROCEDURE IS THE OPPOSITE OF
016200*------- QUANTITYES.  IE:  STR-UM = EA, STR-UM1 = PR, UM1-CF =
016300*------- 2 (2 EACH TO A PAIR).  IF YOU HAVE 2 PAIRS, THEN
016400*------- YOU HAVE 4 EACH.  BUT IF YOU HAVE $2.00 PER PAIR,
016500*------- THEN THE PRICE IS $1.00 EACH.
016600
016700     IF SAVE-RET-CODE = "PR"
016800         IF SOURCE-UM = STR-UM
016900             DIVIDE SOURCE-QTY BY 1
017000               GIVING QTY-STR-UM-DEC ROUNDED
017100             DIVIDE SOURCE-QTY BY 1
017200               GIVING QTY-STR-UM ROUNDED
017300         ELSE
017400         IF SOURCE-UM = STR-UM1
017500             DIVIDE SOURCE-QTY BY STR-UM1-CF
017600               GIVING QTY-STR-UM-DEC ROUNDED
017700             DIVIDE SOURCE-QTY BY STR-UM1-CF
017800               GIVING QTY-STR-UM ROUNDED
017900         ELSE
018000         IF SOURCE-UM = STR-UM2
018100             DIVIDE SOURCE-QTY BY STR-UM2-CF
018200               GIVING QTY-STR-UM-DEC ROUNDED
018300             DIVIDE SOURCE-QTY BY STR-UM2-CF
018400               GIVING QTY-STR-UM ROUNDED
018500         ELSE
018600             MOVE "NF"   TO  RET-CODE
018700             GO TO 6990-MAIN-X
018800     ELSE
018900         IF SOURCE-UM = STR-UM
019000             MULTIPLY SOURCE-QTY BY 1
019100               GIVING QTY-STR-UM-DEC ROUNDED
019200             MULTIPLY SOURCE-QTY BY 1
019300               GIVING QTY-STR-UM ROUNDED
019400         ELSE
019500         IF SOURCE-UM = STR-UM1
019600             MULTIPLY SOURCE-QTY BY STR-UM1-CF
019700               GIVING QTY-STR-UM-DEC ROUNDED
019800             MULTIPLY SOURCE-QTY BY STR-UM1-CF
019900               GIVING QTY-STR-UM ROUNDED
020000         ELSE
020100         IF SOURCE-UM = STR-UM2
020200             MULTIPLY SOURCE-QTY BY STR-UM2-CF
020300               GIVING QTY-STR-UM-DEC ROUNDED
020400             MULTIPLY SOURCE-QTY BY STR-UM2-CF
020500               GIVING QTY-STR-UM ROUNDED
020600         ELSE
020700             MOVE "NF"   TO  RET-CODE
020800             GO TO 6990-MAIN-X.
020900
021000*------- NOW THAT WE HAVE THE QUANTITY OR PRICE IN THE
021100*------- STOREROOM UNIT OF MEASURE, CONVERT INTO INTO
021200*------- ALL THE ALTERNATES
021300
021400     IF STR-UM1 > SPACES
021500         IF SAVE-RET-CODE = "PR"
021600             MULTIPLY QTY-STR-UM-DEC BY STR-UM1-CF
021700               GIVING QTY-STR-UM1 ROUNDED
021800         ELSE
021900             DIVIDE QTY-STR-UM-DEC BY STR-UM1-CF
022000               GIVING QTY-STR-UM1 ROUNDED
022100     ELSE
022200         MOVE ZERO  TO  QTY-STR-UM1.
022300
022400     IF STR-UM2 > SPACES
022500         IF SAVE-RET-CODE = "PR"
022600             MULTIPLY QTY-STR-UM-DEC BY STR-UM2-CF
022700               GIVING QTY-STR-UM2 ROUNDED
022800         ELSE
022900             DIVIDE QTY-STR-UM-DEC BY STR-UM2-CF
023000               GIVING QTY-STR-UM2 ROUNDED
023100     ELSE
023200         MOVE 0  TO  QTY-STR-UM2.
023300
023400     IF DEST-UM > SPACES
023500         IF (DEST-UM = STR-UM) AND (STR-UM NOT = SPACES)
023600             MOVE QTY-STR-UM-DEC  TO  DEST-QTY
023700         ELSE
023800         IF (DEST-UM = STR-UM1) AND (STR-UM1 NOT = SPACES)
023900             MOVE QTY-STR-UM1 TO  DEST-QTY
024000         ELSE
024100         IF (DEST-UM = STR-UM2) AND (STR-UM2 NOT = SPACES)
024200             MOVE QTY-STR-UM2 TO  DEST-QTY
024300         ELSE
024400             MOVE 0           TO  DEST-QTY
024500             MOVE "ND"        TO  RET-CODE
024600     ELSE
024700         MOVE 0               TO  DEST-QTY.
024800
024900 6990-MAIN-X.
025000     GOBACK.
